<p>Port Arthur storm damage claims come from more than hurricanes. A spring squall line can drop hail on Groves, knock a pecan limb through a roof in Port Arthur, and leave a business on Highway 69 without power for two days. A December cold front can spin up a tornado. Each of these is a storm claim, and each can involve several different coverages inside the same policy. This page focuses on how storm claims move from the first phone call to payment, and how to keep them from stalling.</p>

<h2>The Storms That Damage Port Arthur Properties</h2>
<p>NOAA’s Storm Events Database records a steady mix of severe weather in Jefferson County. A few recent examples:</p>
